# Stir Up Trouble aimed at Bot1's own only creature, which is then sacrificed to pay the additional cost (CR 601.2b-h): the
# target is gone by the time the spell resolves, so it does nothing (CR 608.2b) - Bot2's Llanowar Elves lives, and the
# Ornithopter went to the graveyard once, as the cost. Bot1 has only a Swamp, so the sacrifice is the way to pay.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Ornithopter
Stir Up Trouble
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Stir Up Trouble.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Modes(Sacrifice an artifact or creature)
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Stir Up Trouble; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
